  "handoff": "# Handoff — before compact\n\nCreated at: 2026-08-08T22:52:26.896Z\nUpdated at: 2026-08-08T22:52:26.896Z\nReason: before compact\n\n## Progress snapshot\n- Features: 3/11 done, 4 active\n- Phases: 35/93 done, 6 active/discovery\n- Tasks: 199/400 done, 0 active\n\n## Current focus\n- Feature: `2809a7a4-6d53-4a58-b776-bac164bb5d03` — 🛠️ App / Chrome Features (in-progress)\n- Phase: `5cab2dbb-ce1b-4a33-b6bc-ede8437fca09` — app-11: Right-click context menu (in-progress)\n- Task: `479bf80c-6b3d-4e28-8df1-19f509eb3569` — Terminal pane right-click context menu (planned)\n\n## What was being done\nNo additional execution notes were captured.\n\n## Current Task Statuses (phase 5cab2dbb-ce1b-4a33-b6bc-ede8437fca09)\n- 📋 `479bf80c-6b3d-4e28-8df1-19f509eb3569` — Terminal pane right-click context menu (planned)\n- ✅ `967a121b-9003-4abe-bc42-294f25b6fb90` — Build ContextMenu grid-ui widget (done)\n- ✅ `c511a0ad-6883-4b81-a160-c1e6c97516ed` — Sidebar right-click context menu (done)\n\n## How to resume\n1. Open task 479bf80c-6b3d-4e28-8df1-19f509eb3569 (Terminal pane right-click context menu).\n2. Run handoff show <ref> (or /planner handoff show <ref>) to read the phase handoff and compare it with the latest planner data.\n3. Before implementation work, run /planner task start 479bf80c-6b3d-4e28-8df1-19f509eb3569 (or call task_start).\n4. Continue with the next activity: F003/P017 is CLOSED — all nine tasks done 2026-07-27. T009 finished it: the model is now the `heca-view` crate (serde only) and `realize` is `heca-view-realize`, both below the app, and the showcase renders a described tree beside its hand-built twin. The user looked at it in the running app and approved it. Nothing in P017 is open.\n\n## Files to inspect first\n- .planner/project.json\n- .planner/features/\n- .planner/phases/5cab2dbb-ce1b-4a33-b6bc-ede8437fca09.json\n- .planner/phases/cc0308d4-2f40-4516-b389-1422b4aaa7fb.json\n- .planner/.local/resume.json\n- .planner/.local/generated/PLAN.md\n\n## Blockers\n- None recorded\n\n## Next steps\n- F003/P017 is CLOSED — all nine tasks done 2026-07-27. T009 finished it: the model is now the `heca-view` crate (serde only) and `realize` is `heca-view-realize`, both below the app, and the showcase renders a described tree beside its hand-built twin. The user looked at it in the running app and approved it. Nothing in P017 is open.\n- Branch `feat/action-arg-declaration` is PUSHED and **PR #249 is open** (https://github.com/ovidius72/heca/pull/249) — 20 commits, 241 files, +6384/-1702, closing F003/P010 and F003/P017. Whole workspace green (961 tests, 24 suites), clippy 0 warnings at every commit. Awaiting review/merge.\n- F003/P011/T012 (126d0855) is still `blocked`, and its reason needs RE-CHECKING rather than planning around: the 'no chrome surface mounts a ScrollRegion' claim was verified 2026-07-17, and the 2026-07-26 sidebar scroll work may already have discharged it. Its horizontal trigger was settled 2026-07-27 as prefix+Shift+Home/End/PageUp/PageDown — the same four keys as vertical, Shift for the other axis.\n- Unblocked by T009, neither started: F003/P001/T006 (generate widget definitions for JS/Python from `WidgetKind::ALL`, which is a closed list with a coverage guard already walking it) and F003/P011/T006 (the typed builder SDK can now genuinely re-export the model). Also worth checking whether F003/P017/T003's generated property tables are reusable outside the app — they are the natural source for those generated definitions.\n\n## Recent activity\n- 2026-07-29T17:49:33.150Z [task_updated] 2086fbfc-1d37-4e4a-af69-536692ca12cf: Task updated: The mouse: clicking a container focuses it, and each item kind declares its own click\n- 2026-07-29T17:49:32.498Z [task_updated] 2086fbfc-1d37-4e4a-af69-536692ca12cf: Task updated: The mouse: clicking a container focuses it, and each item kind declares its own click\n- 2026-07-29T17:49:31.702Z [task_updated] 2086fbfc-1d37-4e4a-af69-536692ca12cf: Task updated: The mouse: